# Alembic Migrations

## Setup

Migrations are managed using Alembic with async SQLAlchemy support.

## Commands

### Create a new migration

```bash
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "description_of_changes"
```

### Run migrations (upgrade to latest)

```bash
alembic upgrade head
```

### Run migrations (upgrade one step)

```bash
alembic upgrade +1
```

### Downgrade one migration

```bash
alembic downgrade -1
```

### View current revision

```bash
alembic current
```

### View history

```bash
alembic history --verbose
```

## Configuration

- Database URL is read from the `DATABASE_URL` environment variable
- Target metadata is set from `app.models.base.Base.metadata`
- Async engine is used for online migrations
